package ${BASE_PACKAGE}.core.domain

/**
 * Marker interface for use cases — a documentation and grep target that lets reviewer tooling tell
 * use cases from utility classes. Kotlin uses `operator fun invoke`.
 *
 * Conventions (see docs/architecture.md § Visibility):
 * - A use case is a **public** class with a **public `@Inject` constructor**: Hilt builds it in
 *   production, and feature tests build it directly with a fake repository from :core:testing.
 * - **Domain entities take no default values.** Construct them explicitly so call sites state full
 *   intent and every added field is surfaced (DTOs in :core:data may keep wire-format defaults).
 */
interface UseCase
